WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.872
Choosing a summary is a conceptual decision.

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:06.747
Counts and proportions fit nominal categories naturally.

00:00:06.747 --> 00:00:10.902
Ordinal variables often support medians and percentiles.

00:00:10.902 --> 00:00:18.427
Numeric variables may use means and standard deviations when the mean is meaningful and the distribution is

00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:23.822
appropriate. Skewed numeric data often benefits from median and interquartile range.

00:00:23.822 --> 00:00:28.727
Do not apply the same summary mechanically to every column in a dataframe.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:35.582
Connect this idea to a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes.

00:00:35.582 --> 00:00:41.362
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:49.057
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:49.057 --> 00:00:54.842
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:54.842 --> 00:01:00.806
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
